+# SHARE-2 implementation plan
+
+Base: `4534324173e0c8f7e2844c86da60795c32d93da9`.
+
+## Scope and routing
+
+`CommonplaceNext.EditorCell.Mirrors.open/3` gains an explicit
+`{workspace_cell_id, document_id}` target alongside the unchanged path clause.
The explicit target
+sets the canonical Cell in its context, reads the supplied Document directly th
rough the DocSync
+summary/fork lane, and keys the relationship by editor Cell, target Workspace C
ell, and Document.
+The path resolver remains primary-Workspace-only; threading an Organization thr
ough directory
+resolution belongs to ORG-2c and is unnecessary because an explicit target neve
r resolves a path.
+
+The existing `Realm.Route` document-resource branch already selects `Placement.
remote/1` and adds
+the `document_grant` leg for every `EditorCell.sync_verbs/0` verb. The existing
 Gateway client
+already requests, decodes, and spends that frame. Neither file changes: changin
g them would create
+a second route for behavior they already implement. A local target continues th
rough
+`Realm.Router`; a remote target asks the target Realm to authorize and mint, so
 B never asserts A's
+admission decision.
+
+The grant action set remains the SHARE-1 set: `document.read.content` and the s
ync verbs.
+`document.read.history` remains only an in-process DocSync Authority verb and n
o Cell-level decision
+is added for it.
+
+## Verification topology
+
+`Realm.start_for/1` can hold both Workspace Cells in one BEAM, but both use the
 same configured
+SQLite namespace, so that fixture cannot prove the required two-store absence.
The integration
+arms therefore follow `two_organization_test.exs`: A is the parent Workspace Re
alm and B is a child
+BEAM with its own Organization, Workspace Cell, Membership-derived Editor Cell,
 and data directory.
+
+<!-- ARM: S5 B opens A's shared document and edits converge canonically in both
 directions -->
+
+S5 mints A's external grant to B's Editor Cell, opens the target tuple from B,
observes B's edit in
+A's canonical Document, waits for that receipt to settle, then observes a later
 A edit in B's
+mirror. At the base this assertion cannot run green: `git show HEAD` contains o
nly
+`def open(editor, path), do: open(editor, path, [])` and
+`def open(editor, path, options) when is_list(path) and is_list(options)`, so t
he tuple call raises
+`FunctionClauseError`.
+
+<!-- ARM: S6 revoked before open is named and revoked after open stops sync whi
le disclosed content remains -->
+
+S6 verifies the persisted grant is revoked before tuple open and that open retu
rns the named
+`revoked` error without provisioning. It then opens under a replacement grant,
revokes it, edits B
+locally, and observes a blocked mirror within the issuer's 60-second token life
time. The already
+disclosed content remains in B while the new local edit is absent from A.
+
+<!-- ARM: S7 B's shared mirror records A as home and never makes D canonical in
 B's workspace -->
+
+S7 reads B's relationship record and checks both canonical Document references
against D, checks
+D's snapshot home Cell against A, and asks B's independent Workspace store to o
pen D. B reports the
+log absent after the synchronized edit, while B's relationship id remains the o
ne returned by the
+tuple open.
+
+## Preservation
+
+The primary path tests remain unchanged. The old `context/1` descriptor read is
 replaced by
+`context/2` plus the explicit Organization descriptor; the `resolve/2` arity-ze
ro descriptor read
+stays because it defines the unchanged primary path form. The unrelated root-di
rectory descriptor
+read stays untouched. Therefore the corpus count is expected to be 37, not 36.
An added mirror unit
+case also exercises an explicit target whose Workspace Cell is local; it follow
s `Realm.Router`
+and opens without directory resolution.
